From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hemanthkumarm <hemanthkumarm@ami.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Jun 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Run deferred image-object deletes on the main async context

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [AMI-specific customizations]

After a FWUPD_SCRIPT update completes, the staged image object under
/xyz/openbmc_project/software (and its /tmp/images/<id> directory) is removed
by deferring deleteObject->delete_() -> ItemUpdater::erase() ->
deleteImageManagerObject(). The defer was implemented with
boost::asio::post(getIOContext(), ...), which runs the work on a DETACHED
boost::asio io_context thread (see task.cpp). That callback makes blocking
sd_bus calls (ObjectMapper lookup + xyz.openbmc_project.Object.Delete) on the
SAME bus connection the main sdbusplus::async loop owns. sd_bus is not
thread-safe, so this cross-thread use races the main loop and was observed to:

  - fail intermittently with org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.Timeout
    ("Connection timed out") logged by phosphor-image-updater, and
  - silently leave the version object and its /tmp/images directory behind
    (the object remained owned by both xyz.openbmc_project.Software.BMC.Updater
    and xyz.openbmc_project.Software.Version after a successful update).

Fix the root cause by deferring the delete onto the MAIN async context with
ctx.spawn(...) instead of the foreign io_context thread. This still breaks out
of the current call stack (so we never destroy an Activation/Version object
whose method is still on the stack) while keeping every bus call on the
bus-owning thread -- the same pattern already used for the BIOS upgrade path
and by Task. The coroutine takes its state by value (not by capture) to remain
valid across suspension.

This supersedes the earlier "retry the no-reply delete with backoff" workaround:
once the cross-thread race is removed the timeout no longer occurs, and a
blocking retry loop on the async thread would stall the event loop.

Signed-off-by: hemanthkumarm <hemanthkumarm@ami.com>
---
 bmc/activation.cpp   | 19 +++++++++++++------
 bmc/item_updater.cpp | 32 ++++++++++++++++++++++++--------
 2 files changed, 37 insertions(+), 14 deletions(-)

diff --git a/bmc/activation.cpp b/bmc/activation.cpp
--- a/bmc/activation.cpp
+++ b/bmc/activation.cpp
@@ -410,12 +410,19 @@
         Activation::unsubscribeFromSystemdSignals();
     }
 
-    // Delete the uploaded activation
-    auto it = parent.versions.find(versionId);
-    if (it != parent.versions.end())
+    // Delete the uploaded activation on the MAIN async context (not the detached
+    // io_context thread) to avoid racing the shared bus connection -- see
+    // ItemUpdater::flushDeferredDeletes for the full rationale.
+    if (parent.versions.find(versionId) != parent.versions.end())
     {
-        boost::asio::post(getIOContext(),
-                          [it]() { it->second->deleteObject->delete_(); });
+        ctx.spawn([](auto self) -> sdbusplus::async::task<> {
+            auto it = self->parent.versions.find(self->versionId);
+            if (it != self->parent.versions.end())
+            {
+                it->second->deleteObject->delete_();
+            }
+            co_return;
+        }(this));
     }
 }
 
diff --git a/bmc/item_updater.cpp b/bmc/item_updater.cpp
--- a/bmc/item_updater.cpp
+++ b/bmc/item_updater.cpp
@@ -350,17 +350,37 @@
 
 void ItemUpdater::flushDeferredDeletes()
 {
-    for (auto& versionId : deferredDeleteQueue)
+    if (deferredDeleteQueue.empty())
     {
-        boost::asio::post(getIOContext(), [this, versionId]() {
-            auto it = versions.find(versionId);
-            if (it != versions.end())
-            {
-                it->second->deleteObject->delete_();
-            }
-        });
+        return;
     }
+
+    // Run the deferred deletes on the MAIN async context (the thread that owns
+    // the D-Bus connection) rather than on the detached boost::asio io_context
+    // thread. deleteObject->delete_() ultimately makes blocking sd_bus calls
+    // (ObjectMapper lookup + Object.Delete); issuing those from a foreign thread
+    // races with the main sdbusplus::async loop on the shared bus connection and
+    // was observed to fail with org.freedesktop.DBus.Error.Timeout, leaving the
+    // staged image object (and its /tmp/images directory) behind. Spawning onto
+    // ctx still defers the work past the current call stack -- so we never
+    // destroy an Activation/Version object whose method is still executing --
+    // while keeping every bus call on the bus-owning thread.
+    std::vector<std::string> ids(deferredDeleteQueue.begin(),
+                                 deferredDeleteQueue.end());
     deferredDeleteQueue.clear();
+    ctx.spawn(
+        [](ItemUpdater* self,
+           std::vector<std::string> versionIds) -> sdbusplus::async::task<> {
+            for (const auto& versionId : versionIds)
+            {
+                auto it = self->versions.find(versionId);
+                if (it != self->versions.end())
+                {
+                    it->second->deleteObject->delete_();
+                }
+            }
+            co_return;
+        }(this, std::move(ids)));
 }
 
 bool ItemUpdater::requestActivation(std::string& id)
